        <name>Logger</name>
        <qualifiedname>Logger::Logger</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Builds, configures and globally registers the asynchronous logger. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Reads <ref refid="structServerConfig" kindref="compound">ServerConfig</ref> from <ref refid="classConfigurator" kindref="compound">Configurator</ref> (via <ref refid="classStore" kindref="compound">Store</ref>), initialises the spdlog thread pool (queue size THREADPOOL, THREADS workers), builds the console and rotating-file sinks with a shared pattern, adds only the sinks enabled by <computeroutput>log_to_console</computeroutput> / <computeroutput>log_to_file</computeroutput>, then registers the logger as &quot;Project Valhalla&quot; and enables Trantor&apos;s spdlog forwarding. <simplesect kind="post"><para>spdlog has a registered default logger and Trantor routes to it. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="warning"><para>On spdlog_ex (e.g. a duplicate registration) the error is printed to stdout and construction succeeds with logger_ unset; later <ref refid="classLogger_1ad5bca94a0174ce580d9d36c807fbe107" kindref="member">log()</ref> calls would then dereference a null pointer. Construct once, before any component starts logging. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
