    <briefdescription>
<para>Routes Drogon/Trantor log records through an asynchronous spdlog logger. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Owns one spdlog <computeroutput>async_logger</computeroutput> writing to a rotating file sink and/or a colour console sink, selected from <ref refid="classConfigurator" kindref="compound">Configurator</ref>&apos;s <ref refid="structServerConfig" kindref="compound">ServerConfig</ref>. Construction initialises spdlog&apos;s shared thread pool, registers the logger by name, and installs it as both spdlog&apos;s default logger and Trantor&apos;s spdlog backend, so framework, utility and application records all use the same sink configuration.</para>
<para>Intended as a process-wide singleton created by <ref refid="classServer" kindref="compound">Server</ref> through <computeroutput><ref refid="classStore" kindref="compound">Store</ref></computeroutput>; spdlog registration is global, so more than one instance would try to register the same name twice. Logging itself is thread-safe via spdlog&apos;s sinks and worker pool. <simplesect kind="note"><para>The file path is <computeroutput>log_dir</computeroutput> concatenated with <computeroutput>log_file</computeroutput> from <ref refid="structServerConfig" kindref="compound">ServerConfig</ref>; rotation occurs at MAX_LOG_SIZE bytes across MAX_LOG_FILES files. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classMessage" kindref="compound">Message</ref>, <ref refid="classServer" kindref="compound">Server</ref>, <ref refid="classConfigurator" kindref="compound">Configurator</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
